@@ -181,6 +181,118 @@ hg.layer("debug-panel", { exclude = true })
 | `preset` | string | Preset override for this layer |
 | `mask_threshold` | float | Alpha threshold (pixels below this are not glassed). Default `0.001` |
 | `exclude` | bool | Blacklist this namespace instead of whitelisting it |
+| `regions` | table | Declared per-widget slabs, see below |
+| `background` | bool | Glass the visible mask area outside declared regions as a base slab |
+| `pills` | table | Derive dynamic slabs from surface alpha, see below |
+| `debug` | string | Diagnostic render mode: `mask`, `pill_field`, or `attribution` |
+
+#### Declared regions (per-widget slabs)
+
+By default the whole layer surface is one glass slab: widgets in the panel
+interior get the flat middle of that slab and only the panel border shows
+edge effects. Declaring `regions` renders each rectangle as an independent
+slab with its own edges, bezel, refraction center, lens dome and highlights —
+the way first-party glass materials treat each control as its own shape:
+
+```lua
+hg.layer("my-panel", {
+  preset = "panel",
+  regions = {
+    { x = 12,  y = 12, w = 182, h = 64, radius = 6 },
+    { x = 200, y = 12, w = 182, h = 64, radius = 6 },
+    { x = 12,  y = 82, w = 370, h = 48, radius = 6 },
+  },
+})
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `x`, `y` | float | Region top-left, layer-local logical pixels |
+| `w`, `h` | float | Region size, logical pixels |
+| `radius` | float | Corner radius, logical pixels |
+| `blur` | float | Optional per-region blur strength (same units as `blur_strength`); omit to inherit the layer preset. `0` gives clear glass. |
+
+- Lua config only; up to 16 regions per layer (extras are dropped with a warning).
+- `background = true` on the layer renders the mask area *outside* all regions
+  as a whole-surface base slab (a panel sheet behind the widget pills) instead
+  of passing it through unglassed. The sheet's shape comes from the alpha
+  mask, so it follows dynamic layouts. Regions may be nested inside it —
+  attribution picks the innermost containing region.
+- Per-region blur is rendered as extra blurred copies of the sampled
+  background: one additional sample+blur pass per **distinct** `blur` value,
+  capped at 3 distinct values per layer (further values fall back to the
+  preset blur). Reuse values across regions — they share a pass.
+- Glass renders where a region intersects visible content — the alpha mask
+  still applies. Outside all regions the surface renders unglassed. A region
+  that drifts from a dynamic layout therefore degrades to "no glass", never a
+  floating slab over empty space.
+- Each fragment belongs to the nearest region (min SDF), so touching or
+  overlapping regions merge into one continuous slab.
+- The background is sampled and blurred once for the whole layer; regions add
+  no extra blur passes.
+- On rotated/transformed monitors regions fall back to the whole-surface slab.
+
+#### Alpha-derived pills
+
+Pills derive slab geometry from the layer's rendered alpha instead of fixed
+coordinates. Pixels above `threshold` become independent glass controls, so
+the controls follow layout changes without updating configuration:
+
+```lua
+hg.layer("my-panel", {
+  preset = "panel",
+  mask_threshold = 0.001,
+  pills = {
+    threshold = 0.02,
+    bezel = 8,
+    blur = 1.5,
+    corner_lobes = true,
+  },
+})
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `threshold` | float | Surface alpha at which a pixel belongs to a pill. Default `0.02` |
+| `bezel` | float | Edge-effect width in logical pixels. Default `8` |
+| `blur` | float | Optional pill blur strength; omit to inherit the layer preset |
+| `corner_lobes` | bool | Add separated top-left and bottom-right rim reflections. Default `false` |
+
+- Lua config only. Set `threshold` above `mask_threshold` so the lower-alpha
+  panel surface remains a base slab while higher-alpha controls become pills.
+- For a pill-only transparent layer, set `threshold` and `mask_threshold` to
+  the same value. Otherwise lower-alpha antialias pixels around each control
+  intentionally fall through to the base-slab path and can appear as a fringe.
+- The plugin computes a jump-flood distance field from the current surface
+  alpha on every rendered frame. Widget movement and reveal animations do not
+  require declared coordinates.
+- The field's boundary distance and direction form a compact convex bevel with
+  a fixed top-left light. The bevel produces a bright directional rim, narrow
+  glare, and an opposing bottom-right inner shadow while leaving the interior
+  flat and clear.
+- `bezel` controls the bevel width. The active preset's
+  `refraction_strength`, `fresnel_strength`, and `specular_strength` tune its
+  displacement, rim, and glare without changing CSS tint or typography.
+- `corner_lobes` changes only the alpha-derived pills on that layer. Normal
+  windows, declared regions, and pills that leave it disabled are unchanged.
+- Distinct pill and region blur strengths share the same three-variant limit.
+- Pill layers damage their expanded layer box when the surface commits new
+  content, ensuring distance-field changes replace every affected slab.
+- On rotated/transformed monitors pills fall back to the whole-surface slab.
+
+#### Debug modes
+
+Set `debug` on one layer binding to inspect its render inputs without changing
+other namespaces:
+
+| Value | Output |
+|---|---|
+| `mask` | Surface alpha amplified by 50 |
+| `pill_field` | Normalized pill distance field, black near seeds and white at the far limit |
+| `attribution` | Cyan pills, yellow background slab, blue sub-threshold pixels, and white remaining slab pixels |
+
+Debug modes replace the selected layer's normal output and are intended for
+pixel tests and temporary diagnostics.
 
